{"team":"KC","col":"#FF4D57","identity":"pass-heavy","funnel":"balanced-D","plays_pg":61.5,"adot":7.1,"report_html":"<div class=\"report\"><h2>Air Raid</h2><p>This is an aggressive, pass-leaning attack: <strong>+5%</strong> pass rate over expected, top of the league's range, and no interest in sitting on a lead (50% pass when ahead).</p><h3>The Offensive Blueprint</h3><p>There's no bell-cow to bank on \u2014 the lead back sees just <strong>50%</strong> of carries (league ~59%), a committee that caps any one back's ceiling and makes their rushing props matchup- and script-dependent.</p><p><strong>Travis Kelce</strong> is a genuine centerpiece, not an afterthought \u2014 <strong>22%</strong> of targets (league ~15%).</p><p>They spread the ball as much as anyone \u2014 the WR1 commands only <strong>16%</strong> of targets (league ~23%). Volume is democratic here, which suppresses any single receiver's ceiling but props up the TE and secondary options.</p><p>They live in the shotgun (80% of snaps vs ~68%) \u2014 a spread, pass-oriented structure.</p><p>When they fall behind they abandon the run entirely \u2014 61% pass while trailing, so their pass-catchers have huge comeback-script ceilings.</p><p><strong>Patrick Mahomes</strong> is a scramble threat \u2014 he takes off on <strong>4.8%</strong> of dropbacks (nearly double the 3.3% norm), rushing production that both lifts his own yardage and siphons a few carries from the backfield.</p><p>By the numbers it's an efficient unit \u2014 a 46% success rate (above the 44% average).</p><h3>In the Red Zone</h3><p>Their red-zone identity is <strong>pass-first</strong> (56% pass), which puts scoring equity on <strong>Rashee Rice</strong>. And with the TE commanding 22% of targets, <strong>Travis Kelce</strong> is a live red-zone option too.</p><h2>Defense \u2014 No Obvious Seam</h2><p>They lock down opposing WR1s \u2014 just 50 rec yds/game (vs ~58); fade receiving props there.</p><p>They surrender <strong>108 rushing</strong> and <strong>220 passing</strong> yards per game (league ~120 / ~230). No dominant funnel \u2014 read it matchup by matchup.</p><h2>The Betting Angles</h2><p>Bottom line: <strong>Rashee Rice</strong> holds value even when they're winning; their pass-catchers have massive ceilings in comeback scripts (fade-material as underdogs).</p><p><em>Built on 2024\u201325 data; the profile rebuilds through the season as the current staff and roster set their own tendencies.</em></p></div>","depth":{"QB":[{"name":"Patrick Mahomes","slot":"QB1","starter":true,"td":13,"props":{"Comp":22.52,"Att":33.6,"Pass Yds":246.98,"Pass TD":1.82,"INT":0.58,"Rush Yds":19.85},"d":{"completions":22.52,"attempts":33.6,"pass_yards":246.98,"pass_td":1.82,"interceptions":0.58,"rush_att":3.55,"rush_yards":19.85}}],"RB":[{"name":"Kenneth Walker III","slot":"RB1","starter":true,"td":44,"props":{"Rush Att":22.84,"Rush Yds":99.03,"Tgt":4.77,"Rec":3.95,"Rec Yds":30.03},"d":{"rush_att":22.84,"rush_yards":99.03,"targets":4.77,"receptions":3.95,"rec_yards":30.03,"rec_td":0.06}},{"name":"Emmett Johnson","slot":"RB2","starter":true,"td":14,"props":{"Rush Att":3.99,"Rush Yds":16.77,"Tgt":1.7,"Rec":1.14,"Rec Yds":8.03},"d":{"rush_att":3.99,"rush_yards":16.77,"targets":1.7,"receptions":1.14,"rec_yards":8.03,"rec_td":0.04}},{"name":"Brashard Smith","slot":"RB3","starter":false,"td":13,"props":{"Rush Att":4.6,"Rush Yds":16.99,"Tgt":3.19,"Rec":2.06,"Rec Yds":14.03},"d":{"rush_att":4.6,"rush_yards":16.99,"targets":3.19,"receptions":2.06,"rec_yards":14.03,"rec_td":0.07}}],"WR":[{"name":"Rashee Rice","slot":"WR1","starter":true,"td":39,"props":{"Tgt":12.51,"Rec":9.4,"Rec Yds":107.12,"Rec TD":0.52},"d":{"targets":12.51,"receptions":9.4,"rec_yards":107.12,"rec_td":0.52}},{"name":"Xavier Worthy","slot":"WR2","starter":true,"td":20,"props":{"Tgt":6.39,"Rec":4.02,"Rec Yds":49.62,"Rec TD":0.22},"d":{"targets":6.39,"receptions":4.02,"rec_yards":49.62,"rec_td":0.22}},{"name":"Tyquan Thornton","slot":"WR3","starter":true,"td":11,"